WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.090
But in my career, I've just been so fortunate.

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.050
I tell my wife constantly, I'm very lucky.

3
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.490
And I think that luck finds the prepared.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:11.110
But early on,

5
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:12.350
when I was in college,

6
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.520
I worked at a restaurant.

7
00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:17.710
And Chili's is still very popular today.

8
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:19.800
But I had a manager named Howard Kahn,

9
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:20.830
who was a general manager.

10
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.020
And we were the number two

11
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.250
or number three Chili's in all of North America.

12
00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:27.960
And for a general manager

13
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.240
that rolled up his sleeves

14
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:32.580
and could do every position inside of that restaurant

15
00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:33.730
and did every position,

16
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.270
he led by example.

17
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:37.120
And I think that in college,

18
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.890
I saw how he attacked things.

19
00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.720
And he was a major influence

20
00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:43.200
and mentor early on.

21
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.620
And then that led me

22
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:46.400
into my first job out of college.

23
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:47.630
And I got very lucky.

24
00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:48.910
I had Axiom.

25
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:50.380
And I had one of the gentlemen

26
00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.250
who was a head of one of the divisions,

27
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.750
a gentleman by the name of Steve Brighton.

28
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.990
And he was an early mentor of mine.

29
00:00:57.340 --> 00:00:59.020
And I think that the things

30
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.980
that I learned from him with regards

31
00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:03.790
to don't be afraid to take chances.

32
00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:08.550
And it's his tenacity and effort and the culture.

33
00:01:08.780 --> 00:01:09.680
He was a culture builder.

34
00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.000
And I just really learned a lot

35
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.190
about how to build culture from him.

36
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.660
And today, I'd say

37
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.710
that my business partner is a successful investor.

38
00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:23.510
People call their investors, my investor or my chairman.

39
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.180
I'm lucky in that I've got

40
00:01:25.180 --> 00:01:27.280
a business partner who's also the chairman

41
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:29.210
and investor inside of our business.

42
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.220
And I think that learning from his experience

43
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:35.240
and his successes and the things

44
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:36.330
that he's taught me,

45
00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.820
an enormous impact.

46
00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:39.720
And it shows up

47
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.100
at every point along the way.

48
00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:41.750
The integrity.

49
00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:43.630
We had some challenges early on.

50
00:01:44.260 --> 00:01:46.040
And finding a business partner

51
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:49.080
who shoots straight down the middle every time,

52
00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:50.090
no questions asked.

53
00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:51.380
There was a lot of litigation

54
00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:53.090
in our industry early on.

55
00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.090
And we got sued.

56
00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:56.810
I think in the first six months,

57
00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.690
one of our customers got sued.

58
00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.020
And it was frivolous litigation

59
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.250
in the early days of texting.

60
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.480
There's the law that governs.

61
00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.280
This is called the TCPA

62
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.490
or Telephone Consumer Privacy Act.

63
00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:12.590
And there was a lot of gray area.

64
00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:13.980
And it's since been cleaned up

65
00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:17.250
through the Facebook Act of 2021.

66
00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:19.670
And all of that's gone away.

67
00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:20.830
But we got nailed.

68
00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.110
It was quite expensive.

69
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.280
He looked at me, and I looked at him,

70
00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.740
and do we pack up our bags

71
00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:26.830
and call it quits?

72
00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:29.070
Do we put our head down and march forward?

73
00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:31.410
And he said, are we right?

74
00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:32.290
And I said, yes.

75
00:02:32.320 --> 00:02:33.820
And he goes, let's fight it.

76
00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:35.140
And if you feed the pigeons,

77
00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:36.330
they keep coming back.

78
00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:38.070
And I got your back.

79
00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.440
And he showed me

80
00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.650
just what a true partner is.

81
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.630
And held his head high.

82
00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:46.270
And doing the right thing, good things happen.
